{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:QOU.Knot.AngleStructureUniqueness"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Vol_concaveOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Vol_concaveOn","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L243-L264","doc":"**Hypothesis (iv) of `SymmetricOptimum.optima_coincide` for m004, concave\nhalf — DISCHARGED.**  The figure-eight volume functional `totalVol` is concave on\nthe m004 coupled polytope, in the exact `ConcaveOn ℝ m004Polytope totalVol` form\n`optima_coincide` consumes as its `hf₂`.  This is the `ConcaveOn` companion of the\nstrict concavity behind `m004Vol_maximizer_unique`.\n\nBeans `qou-krvm` (iv) / `qou-rvnc` / `qou-7425`.  Two independent single-tetrahedron\nproofs feed the strict concavity this weakens from:\n`QOU.Archimedean.tetVol_strictConcaveOn` (the 2-D simplex route used here, through\n`totalVol_strictConcaveOn`) and `QOU.Knot.Rivin.strictConcaveOn_tetVolLine` (the\nline-parametrised sum-of-squares Hessian, `−cot` on the tangent space of\n`α+β+γ = π`).\n\nWhat (iv) still lacks is **only the geometric identification** — that the analytic\nfunctional `totalVol` IS the hyperbolic volume of the ideal simplex — a\nMostow/Thurston fact Mathlib has no theory for (beans `qou-7y3g`, `qou-idvt` T2).\nThe concavity itself is complete.  Invariance under the concrete m004 symmetry is\nnot needed for m004: strict concavity alone pins the maximiser\n(`m004Vol_maximizer_unique`), so `optima_coincide`'s symmetry route is not the one\nthat closes this anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004_regular_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004_regular_mem","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L231-L241","doc":"**The regular ideal point is feasible for m004** — two regular ideal\ntetrahedra `(π/3, π/3)²`, the radian image of the on-`main` `GA_regular` /\n`Positive_regular`.  A concrete sanity anchor that `m004Polytope` is nonempty and\nfaithfully transcribes the gluing data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.regTet_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.regTet_mem","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L226-L229","doc":"The regular ideal tetrahedron block `(π/3, π/3)` (third angle `π/3`) lies in\nthe open angle simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Vol_maximizer_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Vol_maximizer_unique","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L213-L224","doc":"**The m004 coupled volume has at most one maximiser** — bean `qou-7425`, the\nconcrete multi-tetrahedron discharge of `qou-krvm` (ii) for the figure-eight knot.\nSorry-free, by the generic `totalVol_maximizer_unique` applied to the transcribed\nSnapPy polytope.  (What remains open — the geometric identification that `totalVol`\nIS the hyperbolic volume — is gap 1 in the file header, a sibling-bean matter, not\nsorried here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.convex_m004Polytope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.convex_m004Polytope","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L194-L211","doc":"**The m004 coupled polytope is convex** — the intersection of the two block\nsimplices (each convex, `convex_tetSimplex`) with a hyperplane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Polytope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.m004Polytope","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L188-L192","doc":"The m004 coupled angle polytope (open, radians): both tetrahedron blocks in\nthe open simplex, cut by the single reduced edge equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_symmetric_maximizer_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_symmetric_maximizer_unique","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L160-L176","doc":"**Unique symmetric maximiser of the coupled total volume.**  When a symmetry\n`ρ` stabilises the coupled polytope and leaves `totalVol` invariant, the (unique)\nmaximiser is symmetric — the multi-tetrahedron form of\n`strictConcave_symmetric_maximizer_unique`.  The representation is a hypothesis:\nthe concrete m004 / L6a4 symmetry groups are not built here (see the file header,\ngap 3); for m004, uniqueness needs no symmetry at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_maximizer_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_maximizer_unique","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L146-L158","doc":"**The coupled total volume has at most one maximiser.**  The multi-tetrahedron\nanalytic discharge of `qou-krvm` (ii): on any convex block-in-simplex coupled\npolytope, two maximisers of `totalVol` coincide.  This is what pins the LP optimum\nand the volume-maximising point to a single common point (the vanishing-offset\nexplanation), by strict concavity rather than by the symmetry fixing a lone\npoint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_strictConcaveOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol_strictConcaveOn","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L104-L142","doc":"**The total volume is strictly concave on any convex, block-in-simplex\ncoupled polytope.**\n\nFor a convex feasible set `K ⊆ ι → ℝ × ℝ` on which every tetrahedron's angle\nblock lands in `tetSimplex`, `totalVol` is `StrictConcaveOn ℝ K`.  This is the key\nnew lemma of bean `qou-7425`: a block-separated sum of strictly concave functions\nis strictly concave.  Two distinct feasible points differ in some block `i₀`,\nwhere single-tet strict concavity gives a strict inequality; every other block\ncontributes `≤`; `Finset.sum_lt_sum` makes the total strict.\n\nGeneric in the number of tetrahedra — no assumption on `ι` beyond finiteness, and\nno assumption on `K` beyond convexity and block-membership, so the coupling among\ntetrahedra (the edge equations) is carried entirely by `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.MultiTetVolumeConcave.totalVol","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/MultiTetVolumeConcave.lean#L96-L100","doc":"**Total volume** of a finite family of ideal tetrahedra indexed by `ι`, with\nangle coordinates `x i ∈ ℝ × ℝ` (third angle `π − (x i).1 − (x i).2` implicit):\n`totalVol x = Σ_i tetVol (x i)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}